Package: ubuntu-toolkit
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jaber <jeyaulhoque2025@gmail.com>
Depends: python3, python3-watchdog
Recommends: python3-pil, python3-tqdm, python3-send2trash, python3-pyqt6, libglib2.0-bin
Suggests: libnotify-bin
Installed-Size: 508
Description: seven file-management tools with two systemd user services
 ubuntu-toolkit collects a set of small Python 3 tools for working with
 files in bulk, along with the background jobs and desktop entry that make
 two of them useful without being asked.
 .
 Renaming: bulk-rename and filetool rename many files at once -- prefixes,
 suffixes, find and replace, renumbering, case changes -- and either one can
 undo a run from a shared history log. filetool-gui drives the same engine
 from a window, with a preview table before anything is written.
 .
 Images: filetool image and image-tool compress, resize and convert images
 without touching the originals.
 .
 Duplicates: find-duplicates hashes files across several folders and can
 send the copies it finds to the Trash.
 .
 Downloads: download-organizer sorts loose files in the watched folder into
 subfolders by type, as a systemd user service that waits for a new file to
 stop growing before moving it.
 .
 Wallpaper: bing-wallpaper fetches the day's Bing photo and sets it as the
 GNOME desktop background, as a systemd user service on a daily timer.
 .
 Everything is pure Python 3 and the package contains no compiled code.
 .
 filetool-gui needs a Qt binding, either PySide6 or PyQt6; the latter is
 recommended because Ubuntu 24.04 ships no PySide6.
